"format":"Real LHCb pp collision, 8 TeV, 2012 (run 133488, event 2028034058). Units mm and MeV; LHCb frame (z along the beam into the spectrometer, y up). pvs: [x, y, z, nTracks]. tracks: [type, q, p, nStates, x0, y0, z0, tx0, ty0, then for each further state z, x, y, tx, ty, ..., muon, backward, pvIndex]. type: 1 Velo (VELO only, no momentum: q = p = 0), 3 Long (VELO to T stations, best momentum), 4 Upstream (VELO+TT), 5 Downstream (TT+T, no VELO), 6 Ttrack (T stations only). tx = dx/dz, ty = dy/dz at that state. States are every state the DST stores, sorted by z: ClosestToBeam (near the PV), FirstMeasurement, a V0Vertex state for K0S daughters, BegRich2 at z = 9450 (after the magnet), and for muon candidates the muon-system state at z ~ 12.1-15.3 m. The magnet bends x between the VELO states and z = 9450; y stays nearly straight. muon: 1 = IsMuon. backward: 1 = Velo track flying towards -z (draw from its PV towards negative z). pvIndex: index into pvs (from the PV fit's track list, else the nearest PV by impact parameter). The first nGood tracks are \"good\" (Velo/Long/Upstream/Downstream with ghost probability <= 0.4), sorted by p; the rest are likely ghosts or T-station-only segments. keys: each track's key in event-full.json, same order. v0s: [x, y, z, iA, iB, m_pipi] K0S candidates from the reconstruction (decay vertex, the two daughter track indices, pi+pi- mass; 497.6 = real K0S; the daughters start at the vertex). calo: ECAL energy deposits [x, y, z, E] (shower position at z ~ 12.6 m, energy), one per cluster, ordered as caloCounts: photons (no track), charged (track-matched), split photons of merged pi0s. hcal: [trackIndex, x, y, z, E] HCAL energy along a charged track, placed on that track's straight-line extrapolation to z = 14000 (an assumed mid-HCAL depth). jets: [px, py, pz, m, [trackIndices]] the two jets of the dijet candidate that put this event on the EW stream.",
